12
00:47:31,199 --> 00:47:37,199
My Week with Marilyn is a 2011 biographical film drama directed
by Simon Curtis and written by Adrian Hodges.

13
00:51:28,799 --> 00:51:34,799
It stars Michelle Williams, Kenneth Branagh, Eddie Redmayne, Dominic
Cooper, Julia Ormond, Emma Watson, and Judi Dench.

14
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:32,400
Based on two books by Colin Clark, it depicts the making of the 1957 film The Prince and the
Showgirl, which starred Marilyn Monroe (Williams) and Laurence Olivier (Branagh).

15
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
The film concerns the week during the shooting of the film when Monroe was escorted around London by Clark
(Redmayne), after her husband Arthur Miller (Dougray Scott) had returned to the United States.

16
01:03:21,599 --> 01:03:27,599
Principal photography began on 4 October 2010, at Pinewood Studios.

17
01:07:19,199 --> 01:07:25,199
Filming took place at Saltwood Castle, White Waltham
Airfield, and on locations in and around London.

18
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:22,800
Curtis also used the same studio in which Monroe had
shot The Prince and the Showgirl in 1956.

19
01:15:14,399 --> 01:15:20,399
My Week with Marilyn had its world premiere at the New York Film Festival on 9 October
2011, and was shown at the Mill Valley Film Festival two days later.

20
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film was released on 23 November 2011, in the United
States, and on 25 November in the United Kingdom.

21
01:23:09,599 --> 01:23:15,599
The film received generally positive reviews and grossed $35 million worldwide.

22
01:27:07,199 --> 01:27:13,199
Williams and Branagh were nominated for the Academy Awards for
Best Actress and Best Supporting Actor respectively.

23
01:31:04,800 --> 01:31:10,800
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship, countryside,
based on novel or book, cinema on cinema, movie business.

24
01:35:02,399 --> 01:35:08,399
The tone is emotional.
